Workshop is a large and luminous room. There are lots of incomprehensible devices and tools. Nikolas, dressed in black overall is standing by the workbench, grinding some part with a file. You can see something, a cross between a dummy and a knight`s armour standing near the workbench . There are gears in figure's chest.
"Father calls him a golem", whispers Doyle. "He's joking, of course, golems exist only in tales. This is a robot."
"A robot?" you ask, "can it think?".
"No, not yet. It's difficult to make a machine which is able to think by itself. Father will operate it from the control panel".
"And what is that?" you ask pointing at a flat metal box with round metal wheel on one side.
"We have called it a lighter," says Doyle, "there is benzine inside. When you turn the wheel, sparks are produced, and benzine catches fire. It`s more convenient than matches".
"Shall we take it, just in case?"
"Ok".
Doyle puts the lighter in his pocket. At the same time Nikolas notices you.
"Hello, boys!" he smiles. "Would you like me to tell you about my golem?".
You unnoticeably pull Doyle's sleeve, but it's too late. You don't want to offend Nikolas, so you patiently listen to him. Time flies and you constantly look at the clock. And finally, when the moment is right, you make an excuse, and say that you have to go.  